---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Controller details (Companies House). ICO registration to be added once the
// data-protection fee is paid — see the TODO below.
const ENTITY = "THE MARKETING EXPERTS (NATIONWIDE) LTD";
const COMPANY_NO = "15221860";
const ADDRESS = "5 Regent Street, Rugby, Warwickshire, CV21 2PE, United Kingdom";
const EMAIL = "hello@tmke.co.uk";
const UPDATED = "16 June 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — TMKE"
  description="How TMKE (The Marketing Experts (Nationwide) Ltd) collects, uses and protects your personal data."
  noindex
>
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="legal-inner">
      <p class="legal-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains how <strong>{ENTITY}</strong> (“TMKE”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses and
        protects your personal data when you use our website, enquire about or buy our services, or
        otherwise deal with us. We are the “controller” of your personal data under the UK GDPR and the
        Data Protection Act 2018.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Company:</strong> {ENTITY} (trading as TMKE)</li>
        <li><strong>Registered in England &amp; Wales, company no.</strong> {COMPANY_NO}</li>
        <li><strong>Registered office:</strong> {ADDRESS}</li>
        <li><strong>Contact for data matters:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></li>
        <li><strong>ICO registration:</strong> [to be confirmed — registration in progress]</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. The information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use the site, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry &amp; contact details</strong> — your name, email address, phone number,
          company name and any message you send us through our forms (for example brochure requests,
          discovery-call bookings and contact forms).</li>
        <li><strong>Account information</strong> — if you create an account, your name, email, company
          and login credentials (passwords are handled by our authentication provider and are not visible
          to us).</li>
        <li><strong>Booking &amp; service information</strong> — details you provide to plan and deliver
          work, including locations/addresses for videography, project briefs and agreement records.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment information</strong> — where you pay for services, payment is processed by our
          payment provider; we receive confirmation and limited transaction details, not your full card
          number.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage &amp; analytics data</strong> — if you consent to analytics cookies, we record
          pages visited, referring page, and a randomly-generated session identifier so we can understand
          how the site is used. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — your IP address and basic device/browser information,
          collected by our hosting and security providers to deliver and protect the site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we use your data, and our lawful basis</h2>
      <table class="legal-table">
        <thead><tr><th>What we do</th><th>Lawful basis (UK GDPR)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Respond to your enquiry and provide a quote</td><td>Legitimate interests / steps prior to a contract</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Deliver our services, manage your account and bookings</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Take payment and keep accounting/tax records</td><td>Contract and legal obligation</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Run, secure and improve the website (incl. fraud/abuse prevention)</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Analytics cookies and similar storage</td><td>Consent</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Marketing emails about our services</td><td>Consent (or, for existing customers, our legitimate interest in the “soft opt-in”)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We use strictly-necessary cookies/storage to make the site work (for example to keep you signed in
        and to protect against abuse), and — only with your consent — analytics storage to understand usage.
        You can accept or reject non-essential storage at any time. Full details are in our
        <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share your data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with service providers who process it on our
        behalf under contract, including providers of:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>website hosting, content delivery and security;</li>
        <li>our database and account authentication;</li>
        <li>email delivery (transactional and, where you’ve consented, marketing);</li>
        <li>payment processing and accounting;</li>
        <li>mapping/distance calculation (for travel estimates), where relevant; and</li>
        <li>customer-relationship and analytics tools.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose data where required by law, or to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.
      </p>

      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some of our providers are based outside the UK (including in the United States). Where personal data
        is transferred outside the UK, we rely on an appropriate safeguard — such as a UK “adequacy”
        regulation (including the UK Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is
        certified) or the UK International Data Transfer Agreement / Standard Contractual Clauses — so your
        data receives an equivalent level of protection.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiries that don’t become customers:</strong> typically up to 24 months after our last
          contact, then deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Customer &amp; account records:</strong> for the life of the relationship and a reasonable
          period afterwards.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial/transaction records:</strong> 6 years, to meet HMRC and accounting requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> retained for a limited period and then aggregated or deleted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="legal-note">(These periods are our standard defaults and may be confirmed/adjusted following legal review.)</p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data erased, in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to our processing, in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>data portability; and</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, where we rely on consent (this won’t affect processing already carried out).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. We’ll respond within one month.</p>

      <h2>9. Marketing</h2>
      <p>
        We’ll only send you marketing where you’ve agreed, or where the law otherwise allows it for existing
        customers. You can opt out at any time using the unsubscribe link in any marketing email, or by
        emailing us.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including access
        controls and encryption in transit. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure,
        but we work to protect your information and have procedures to deal with any suspected breach.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>Our services are aimed at businesses and are not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect data about children.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. We’ll change the “last updated” date above and, where appropriate, tell you.</p>

      <h2>13. How to contact us or complain</h2>
      <p>
        For any privacy question or to exercise your rights, contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your data you can
        also complain to the UK regulator, the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO):
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>,
        helpline 0303 123 1113.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-foot"><a href="/">&larr; Back to TMKE</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
